WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.560
The mind-blowing finale of I Am Not Okay With
This left us with so many questions about

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.410
Syd's powers and the identity of the mysterious
figure.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:12.600
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video, I'll be breaking all of that down,

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.110
and explaining the secret conspiracy that
led to Syd's superpowers, plus Season 2 theories.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.380
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care if
you haven't seen the show yet.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:26.300
The first season ends with a literal bang
when Syd's powers explode Brad's head at the

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.539
school Homecoming.

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:32.210
As gruesome as it is, it's also designed to
be kind of funny because Brad unsuspectingly

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:35.040
predicted his own demise earlier that same
day:

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.410
"Let's just say that tonight's gonna be f***ing
mind-blowing."

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.650
When Syd flees the scene, she returns to the
tower that she went to the previous time her

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.910
powers became massively out of control.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:49.280
As she contemplates her future, we hear whispering
voices and a dark cloud of particles arrives

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.280
on the platform behind her, taking on a human
form.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.280
"Who are you?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.280
Should I be afraid?

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.280
They should be afraid."

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.290
So, who is this strange, shadowy figure that's
been stalking Syd?

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:03.909
This entity can dissolve into a dark cloud
as we saw when it was watching Syd after her

00:01:03.909 --> 00:01:05.790
training session with Stan.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:10.410
On the one hand, the show seems to hint it
could be her father or a vision of him.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:14.390
For example, when Syd mentions to her school
counsellor that she thought a man had been

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.390
following her, Ms. Cappriotti asks Syd if
it looked like her father.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:22.430
And basically suggests that the figure was
just a grief hallucination of her dead dad

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.830
caused by her feelings of loss over him.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:29.340
However, when this mystery figure finally
appears in front of Syd on the platform, she

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.890
doesn't recognise him.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:35.270
We also know that Syd's mother said that when
her father was still alive, he believed somebody

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:36.870
was following him too.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:41.310
Curiously, in the graphic novel that the show
is based on, a shadowy, black form appears

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.330
in a scene where Syd is having sex.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:47.960
And in the comic, it's Syd's powers which
unconsciously create this menacing entity.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:52.900
So, in the TV show, could this ghostly figure
be something that Syd has created from her

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.730
inner abilities without realising?

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:59.790
When Syd and Stan are reviewing the stolen
library security cam footage, Stan even comments,

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.659
"That just looks like your shadow."

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:06.659
Whoever or whatever it might be, the ending
is setting this mystery man up as a mentor

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.640
figure for Syd in the second season.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:14.060
Stan, who already thinks of Syd as a superhero,
pointed out to her that this is classic comic

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.060
book storytelling.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.920
"So each of these comics features an unknown
visitor.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.500
A professor, a wise old sage, some form of
mentor figure,

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.530
you know, who visits the hero,
explains their abilities, the mythology behind

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.030
them,
and how they can harness those powers for

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.030
good."

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:32.360
This being is likely there to help Syd properly
understand how to control her powers, and

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.570
maybe even harness them in a positive way.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:42.920
"I mean, if I really can make a nose bleed
with my brain, then maybe it can be used for

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:43.920
good."

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.240
So far, Syd's struggled to manage her powers.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.900
She's tried blocking out negative thoughts
and smoking weed which seem to help somewhat.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.720
But these aren't real, permanent solutions
as any type of strong emotion or panic trigger

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:59.650
her powers in unpredictable and dangerous
ways.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:04.739
Season 1 then is Syd's superhero origin story,
and the show heavily hints that she received

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:06.160
them from her father.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.650
When Stan tries to figure out how Syd got
her powers, he suggests that

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:12.630
"Sometimes a person inherits their abilities."

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:16.660
And Syd's mother also tells her
"When it comes to your dad, you have this

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:17.660
gift."

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.190
There are also obvious parallels in terms
of their shared telekinetic powers between

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:25.570
Syd and Eleven from Stranger Things whose
own powers originate from the clandestine

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:28.720
MK Ultra experiments carried out on her mother.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.660
However, the origin of Syd's father's powers
is, as yet, unknown.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.550
In fact, the show's co-creator and director,
Jonathan Entwistle has said that "there is

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.630
[…] a much bigger, under-the-surface conspiracy
[to do with the powers] that goes back much

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:42.630
further."

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:46.540
Which makes me wonder whether Syd's father
was experimented on by the military after

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.340
he joined the marines?

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:52.460
And when Stan is trying to figure out the
origin for Syd's powers, one of the possibilities

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.150
he mentions is
"Secret military experiment?"

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:59.690
Syd's father could have been involved in covert
military research and trials designed to turn

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.709
him into a kind of super-soldier.

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:05.599
One of the best-known comic book characters
who underwent this type of experiment is Steve

00:04:05.599 --> 00:04:08.230
Rogers, aka Captain America.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:12.849
Another hint towards experimentation or perhaps
a chemical accident being the cause of her

00:04:12.849 --> 00:04:16.470
father's powers is that we get a number of
scenes in Syd's chemistry class.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:22.650
"As the temperature increases, if an atom
loses one or more electrons, it becomes oxidized!"

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:27.410
And the blackboard behind him is also filled
with numerous details about acid and alkaline

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.439
reactions.

00:04:28.439 --> 00:04:33.270
We also learn that during her father's final
tour, he was the only human being who survived

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.650
an enormous explosion.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:39.889
What if that explosion was set off by some
kind of bio-weapon that triggered a mutation

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:40.889
in him?

00:04:40.889 --> 00:04:44.689
Alternatively, the explosion might have gone
off next to a chemical facility and killed

00:04:44.689 --> 00:04:47.259
everyone else but gave him powers?

00:04:47.259 --> 00:04:51.139
Or perhaps he'd already been experimented
on, along with others, and the explosion was

00:04:51.139 --> 00:04:55.499
deliberately engineered to test whether any
of them would survive the blast, and only

00:04:55.499 --> 00:04:56.610
he did.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:01.159
X-Men characters like Wolverine and Deadpool
received superhuman healing abilities after

00:05:01.159 --> 00:05:02.430
being experimented on.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:08.050
In fact, I Am Not Okay With This has numerous
allusions to the X-Men from Stan's "Not Men"

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:11.069
comic book,
the Wolverine-like spiked gloves that Syd's

00:05:11.069 --> 00:05:16.569
brother designs for his superhero suit,
and the school is also "Home of the Wolverines".

00:05:16.569 --> 00:05:21.139
Comic book characters have often received
their powers through accidents or mutations.

00:05:21.139 --> 00:05:25.740
Daredevil got his powers when he was blinded
during a chemical accident and Carol Danvers,

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:30.419
aka Captain Marvel, was an ordinary human
who received her powers when she absorbed

00:05:30.419 --> 00:05:33.729
the energy from an experimental light-speed
engine that blew up.

00:05:33.729 --> 00:05:39.020
And there's also Stan's "Spider Tales" comic,
referencing the radioactive arachnid bite

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.150
that gave Spider-Man his abilities.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.809
At the end of the season, when the mystery
figure tells Syd

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:47.270
"They should be afraid"
he could be referring to the people involved

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.539
in the conspiracy rather than the townspeople.

00:05:49.539 --> 00:05:54.009
For example, if it is the ghost of her father,
he could be looking for revenge.

00:05:54.009 --> 00:05:58.460
He could have even been murdered and his death
made to look like a suicide, remember he never

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.009
left a note.

00:06:00.009 --> 00:06:04.990
Another possibility is that there are supernatural
or even alien forces at play here, given the

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.590
mystery man's ability to disappear into thin
air.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:11.960
There's a hint to this in the poster for the
movie They Came From Beyond Space which is

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.550
displayed quite prominently in Stan's room.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:19.400
In that movie, space aliens attempt to enslave
humans by possessing them.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.419
Whether Syd will be able to keep her powers
under the radar in the second season is unclear

00:06:23.419 --> 00:06:27.219
because her diary which Brad was reading out
went missing on the dance floor during the

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:28.969
panic after his head exploded.

00:06:28.969 --> 00:06:34.120
It'll be interesting to see how Brad's death
is explained by investigators, but some suspicion

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:38.360
may fall on Syd given how he was ranting at
her just before he died.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:42.749
Especially if her diary ends up in the hands
of someone who decides to reveal her secret

00:06:42.749 --> 00:06:47.680
to fellow students, teachers, or the police,
or perhaps even ends up blackmailing her about

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:48.680
it.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:53.050
Now, if you've read the original graphic novel,
you might be thinking that ultimately Syd's

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:57.520
journey will end in tragedy, because...
spoilers for the comic book...,

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.360
Syd commits suicide when she discovers she
can't handle her powers.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:06.249
However, Entwistle has specifically said that
the Netflix version of the story will not

00:07:06.249 --> 00:07:10.470
be as "macabre" and will instead expand the
world of the graphic novel.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:15.020
To be honest, a suicide storyline as the final
destination for Syd would be a rather bleak

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:20.020
way to treat a character who's not only grappling
with grief, but also confronting her burgeoning

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:25.669
sexuality and feelings of social isolation,
who could hopefully still find a path to dealing

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:26.669
with all that.

00:07:26.669 --> 00:07:30.939
Entwistle has also said that while the comic
is "a story about mental illness, and essentially

00:07:30.939 --> 00:07:35.379
suicide", what he wanted to do with the show
was build out "the backstory of how [Syd]

00:07:35.379 --> 00:07:38.369
got [to that point]"
and "take all the elements of a journey of

00:07:38.369 --> 00:07:41.649
somebody being confused by lots of different
things in their life [..]

00:07:41.649 --> 00:07:44.129
and make a different type of genre show."

00:07:44.129 --> 00:07:48.439
So, did the ending of I Am Not Okay With This
blow your mind?

00:07:48.439 --> 00:07:50.499
And who do you think the mystery figure is?

00:07:50.499 --> 00:07:53.349
Leave your thoughts and theories in the comments
below.

00:07:53.349 --> 00:07:57.129
If you enjoyed this, then a thumbs-up and
a share are hugely appreciated.

